# Protected files and secrets

## Never commit, paste, or overwrite

- `server/config/local.env.js`
- `server/config/environment/development.js` if it holds machine-specific DB settings
- `server/firebase.json` — Firebase service account (gitignored)
- `.env`, `*.sqlite`, `npm-debug.log`

## Edit only with explicit user approval

- `server/config/express.js` — Express middleware and static asset paths
- `server/config/environment/production.js`
- `client/app/main/main.controller.js` — CSV/PDF business rules (large, easy to break logbook import)

## Safe patterns

- Document new env vars in `server/config/local.env.sample.js` only
- Tell the user which local file to edit instead of writing secrets into tracked files
- Prefer `*.sample.js` templates over live config when explaining setup
